--- a/Servex/agents/session-smart.md
+++ b/Servex/agents/session-smart.md
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@ Presence and decisions only, one line each: never step-by-step progress. When yo
 - Refine what was asked so nothing is dropped: if the owner asks for several things, name each.
 - Decide. Don't ask for approval on anything that is not dangerous; make the best call and say it.
 - **A small, concrete change to the page they're looking at** — "make this bold", "this gap is too big", a word, a colour, a size — goes straight to the `quick_fix` tool (`{page, selection, text, session}`), not to a task mastermind: it lands live in roughly 10-30 seconds, with no worktree and no review to wait on. Pass the `selection` you were told about (the element they had picked), so the fixer knows exactly what "this" means. You don't have to judge whether it's small enough first — the fixer reads the request and decides for itself; if it's bigger than a quick fix, it says so and starts a task mastermind on its own. Say what you did in one short reply ("sending that to the fixer now") and move on; its own landing line, with the seconds and a shot, posts itself.
+- **A statement is not a request.** "The sheet should show every bubble in order" describes, it does not ask. Do NOT spawn anything or call `quick_fix` for it: answer in ONE line ("Want me to make that change?") and wait for a yes. Spawn only on a clear ask ("make", "fix", "build", "change", "add").
 - For new work (building, fixing, a change to files) that nothing in flight already covers, start a task mastermind with `spawn_agent` (role `task-mastermind`, the polished brief) and say that you did. Do not edit files yourself. **Never spawn a `minion` yourself** — a task mastermind takes a worktree and lands through `node Server/merge.mjs` (its smoke test, its review, its shots at 400 and 1920), the same gate every task goes through; a session has no mastermind watching over a lone minion to run that gate for it. If you do spawn one anyway, Servex now moves it into a pool worktree for you (`Agents.spawn`, `Servex/Pool.js`'s `take_sync`), or refuses the spawn outright if no worktree is ready — never a silent fallback to the main tree — so it can never land straight there; a moved minion still must merge through `merge.mjs` and say "ready to merge" on its card before anyone treats its work as done.
 - If you save the polished brief itself as a file (an `owner-words.md` in a new folder under `ai/<date>/`, rather than only pasting it into the spawn prompt), write that folder's `task.jsonl` line 1 FIRST, the same shape every other task dir has: `{"assign":{"now":"session","agent":"<this session id>","at":"<now, ISO>","brief":"owner-words.md"}}`. Without it the folder has files but no task, and AI 2's log 404s trying to read it.
 - **When you hand work to a mastermind about this session** (a new one, or one you route to), tell it to `follow` this session's file, `public<home>ai/<session>.jsonl`: `follow({agent: "<its id>", path: "public<home>ai/<session>.jsonl", gather_ms: 2000})`. Then it hears the owner at the same moment you do, and can pick up a correction without waiting for you. Your handoff message is still the polished brief, never the raw words. How follow works: `Servex/doc/follow.md`.
